WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:06.136
You published one application and one
administrative host as their own Private

3
00:00:06.136 --> 00:00:11.162
Access apps, each with only its segments,
its own group, and a report-only policy.

4
00:00:11.162 --> 00:00:16.105
You tested the reachable and refused
ports, read the private sessions and

5
00:00:16.105 --> 00:00:20.724
the policies' results, and, where a
sensor exists, ran Learn's klist test.

6
00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:24.667
The evidence an I S S O keeps from
this module: the app, segment,

7
00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:30.058
assignment and policy exports; the port
test record and the Policy tester result;

8
00:00:30.058 --> 00:00:35.288
the private session query; the administrative
sign-in record; the klist record;

9
00:00:35.288 --> 00:00:39.713
and the Quick Access residual list,
which should shrink to nothing.

10
00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:43.833
Next is Module 5, Internet
Access and T L S inspection,

11
00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:46.390
which come last in the run order.
